---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Deliberately non-technical: nothing here names the stack, the pipeline,
// or how drafting works. It's a reader-facing page about editorial
// standards, not a colophon.
//
// The AI wording is load-bearing. "AI-assisted and human-moderated", with
// the human role described as judgement over what's covered/published/
// corrected rather than a per-article review promise, stays true both
// today (every piece is checked before merge) and under a more hands-off
// approach later. Don't tighten it into "every article is reviewed by a
// human" -- that's a promise the site would then have to keep.
//
// Origin info is kept to exactly what /privacy/ already says: a non-profit
// publication operated from Finland. Nothing further about who operates it.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Chessori"
  description="What Chessori publishes, how stories are chosen, and how the site handles photos, AI and corrections."
  activeContinent="about"
>
  <header class="section-head">
    <h1>About Chessori</h1>
    <p>What this site is, and how it works</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Chess is well covered already. What's harder to find is the second read: the piece that tells you why a
      result matters, what it echoes, or where the money actually went.
    </p>

    <p>
      That's what this site is for. When something happens in chess, we link you to whoever reported it first, then
      publish our own companion piece alongside it. A historical parallel, the economics, the reaction, or what the
      tournament numbers actually show. Never a reworded version of someone else's article. If you only want the
      news itself, follow the source link. It's on every page, twice.
    </p>

    <h2>How stories get picked</h2>
    <p>
      A handful a day, no more. We'd rather publish three things worth reading than everything that happened.
      Stories are chosen on how much there is genuinely new to say about them, and the ones we'd only be repeating
      get dropped.
    </p>

    <h2>Photos</h2>
    <p>
      Every photo comes from Wikimedia Commons under a licence that allows reuse, credited to the photographer,
      with a link back to the original file. We don't take images from the outlets we link to.
    </p>

    <h2>AI, and people</h2>
    <p>
      Chessori's articles are AI-assisted and human-moderated. The tools do a lot of the writing. The judgement
      stays with people: what's worth covering, what gets published, and what gets fixed when it turns out to be
      wrong.
    </p>

    <h2>When we get it wrong</h2>
    <p>
      We will, eventually. Every article has a link at the foot for reporting an error, and it reaches a person.
      Corrections get made, not quietly buried.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      Chessori is a non-profit publication operated from Finland. You can reach us any time through the
      <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section-head {
    padding: 34px 0 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .section-head h1 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 540;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 44px);
  }
  .section-head p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  /* Same measure and left alignment as /privacy/ -- .section-head spans
     the full width, so a centred column would leave the h1 stranded out
     to the left of its own body text. */
  .prose {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 30px 0 60px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .prose .lede {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1.1em;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 540;
    font-size: 24px;
    margin: 1.8em 0 0.45em;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1em;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
